---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Ashish Koka — ME Computer Science student at University of Cincinnati, software engineer, and IEEE-published researcher."
>
  <section class="about-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="about-hero__label reveal">
        <span class="section-label">About</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="about-hero__title reveal reveal-delay-1">
        Building software<br/>
        <span class="gradient-text">that holds up.</span>
      </h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-body">
    <div class="container about-body__grid">

      <div class="about-body__content prose reveal">
        <p>
          I'm Ashish Koka — a software engineer and graduate student in Computer Science at the
          University of Cincinnati. I completed my B.Tech in Computer Science Engineering at
          SRM University AP (CGPA 3.2/4.0), and I'm now pursuing my Master of Engineering
          while building real projects in data engineering, systems programming, and ML.
        </p>
        <p>
          My work spans the stack: from C-level virtual memory simulators and machine learning
          algorithms implemented from scratch in NumPy, to full-stack analytics dashboards
          deployed on Azure SQL. I've also published research at IEEE on applying deep learning
          to medical prediction problems.
        </p>
        <p>
          I care about understanding things at a level below the abstraction. That's why I
          implement SMO before I use sklearn, and why I build the VM manager before I study the
          OS page-replacement chapter. Reaching for a library is fast; knowing what it's doing
          is better.
        </p>

        <h2>Experience</h2>
        <p>
          I interned as a <strong>Software Engineer at IntegrAuth</strong>, where I worked with
          authentication, authorization, and identity access management tools. Before that, I
          completed a <strong>Salesforce Developer internship</strong>, building familiarity with
          the platform's development model through guided courses and hands-on exercises.
          Outside engineering, I've worked as a <strong>Front Desk Assistant</strong> at the
          University Sports Association, which taught me how much of good work is about
          communication and follow-through.
        </p>

        <h2>Research</h2>
        <p>
          I published a paper at IEEE titled <em>"Deep Learning Approach on Prediction of
          Tinnitus"</em> — applying deep learning methods to a medical prediction problem.
          That work shaped how I think about data quality, model evaluation, and the gap between
          academic benchmarks and real-world deployment constraints.
        </p>

        <h2>Outside of code</h2>
        <p>
          I was a member of the SRMAP movie club management team and helped supervise short film
          competitions. I've coordinated stalls at university fests. I find that the communication
          skills from that kind of work transfer directly to engineering — presenting ideas clearly,
          running a retrospective, knowing when to push and when to wait.
        </p>
      </div>

